{"explanation":"If interest is compounded n times a year, each period adds 1/n of 100%, so after one year your $1 becomes (1 + 1/n)^n. Yearly compounding gives $2, monthly about $2.613, daily about $2.7146, and every minute about $2.71828. The more often it compounds, the more money you get, but the gains get smaller each time, and the total never goes past one value: e ≈ 2.71828. In the limit (continuous compounding), the balance at time t is exactly e^t. Use the slider to change how often interest is added and watch the staircase close in on the smooth yellow curve. Click "Animate" to step through every frequency.","manimCode":"const ax = new Axes({ xRange: [0, 1, 0.25], yRange: [0, 3, 0.5], xLength: 7, yLength: 5, tips: false });
ax.moveTo([-1, -0.4, 0]);
scene.add(ax);

const xl = new Text({ text: 'time (years)', color: GRAY, fontSize: 20 });
xl.moveTo(ax.c2p(0.5, -0.35));
const yl = new Text({ text: 'balance ($)', color: GRAY, fontSize: 20 });
yl.moveTo(ax.c2p(-0.13, 3.05));
scene.add(xl, yl);

// continuous limit e^t
const expCurve = ax.plot(t => Math.exp(t), { color: YELLOW, xRange: [0, 1], numSamples: 200 });
scene.add(expCurve);

// horizontal line at e
const eLine = new Polygon({ vertices: [ax.c2p(0, Math.E), ax.c2p(1, Math.E)], color: YELLOW_D });
eLine.setStrokeWidth(1.5).setFillOpacity(0);
scene.add(eLine);
const eLab = new MathTex({ latex: 'e \\approx 2.71828', color: YELLOW });
await eLab.waitForRender();
eLab.scale(0.7);
